title: A spice for every port
from: Chef Auda Brennan
gist: Brennan's small talk on the spices she brought away from every port, and the shelf in her galley.
== lines
brennan: Hello, loves. Have you eaten? Don't answer. There's a tray of biscuits going round.   [gesture]
brennan: Every port I've cooked in, I brought one spice away. Like a postcard you can eat.
brennan: Marra Station: smoked salt from a stall in the rain. The man wouldn't tell me what wood.
brennan: Port Halloran: the pepper the fishing boats use. Hot enough to dry your socks.   [laugh]
brennan: My mum says add a spice until the pan sounds right. Annoying. Also right.
brennan: Half the jars on my shelf came from you lot. Every jar's got a story.   [nod]
brennan: Right. Questions, loves. Then more biscuits.
? choice
* Which spice is your favourite?   rel:brennan+2 flavour:share mem:talk.brennan.asked
  brennan: The smoked salt. One pinch and the whole mess goes quiet. Best sound there is.   [nod]
* Can I bring one for the shelf?   rel:brennan+2 flavour:practical mem:talk.brennan.asked
  brennan: Course, love. Next port, find a stall and bring me something I've never tasted.   [laugh]
* (Just listen)
  brennan: No questions? Then eat. That's the rule in here too.
brennan: Thank you, loves. Off you go, and eat something.
